# Why this file exists (Phase 118 / CONF-01, plan 118-02 Task 1):
#
# `engines.node` in package.json is only a DECLARATION. Without engine-strict,
# npm prints an `EBADENGINE` warning and installs anyway. The install would then
# "succeed" on Node 20 and the suite would die at first invocation with:
#
#   SyntaxError: The requested module 'fs' does not provide an export named 'globSync'
#
# `@modelcontextprotocol/conformance` imports `globSync` from `node:fs` at module
# scope (Node >= 22) and declares no `engines` of its own, so npm has nothing to
# check unless this repo declares it and then makes the declaration binding.
#
# The setting below is what converts that declaration into an ENFORCEMENT:
# `npm ci --prefix conformance --ignore-scripts` now exits non-zero on Node 20.
# The refusal is proved by execution, not assumed - see 118-02-SUMMARY.md.
engine-strict=true
